-- Reconcile migration history with schema.prisma (finding P0-1 / MG-1).
--
-- Before this migration, `prisma migrate deploy` on an empty database produced
-- a schema the application could not run against: these tables and columns
-- existed only in schema.prisma (presumably applied to dev databases with
-- `db push`). This migration is generated by `prisma migrate diff` and is
-- additive:
--   * creates 5 tables (email_verification_tokens, password_reset_tokens,
--     mfa_codes, mfa_verifications, saved_payment_methods) with FKs + indexes
--   * adds users.failed_login_attempts (constant default, metadata-only on
--     PG 11+), users.locked_until, patient_profiles.stripe_customer_id (nullable)
--   * adds the missing (shift_id, queue_position) index
--   * drops the database-side id / updated_at defaults on the five tables from
--     20261023000000; Prisma supplies these values client-side, as it does for
--     every other table. Metadata-only, reversible with SET DEFAULT.
--
-- Nothing is dropped or rewritten. On a database where some of these objects
-- were already created by `db push`, resolve with
-- `prisma migrate resolve --applied 20261023180000_reconcile_schema_drift`
-- after checking `prisma migrate diff` is empty.

